        moat: "Scale and compliance: large clients do not want the legal risk of moving thousands of workers to a smaller vendor, and every tightening of labour rules has pushed work towards the biggest players. The weakness is pricing power: a normal general-staffing contract earns a mark-up of only about ₹600–700 per worker, and clients can re-tender.",
